1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,697
Every Indian could stand inside one city.

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:09,060
Over 1.4 billion people, packed two to a square meter, the safe limit at a concert,

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:12,069
fill a square just 27 kilometers wide.

4
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:15,461
Pour it into Delhi, and it fills only half the city.

5
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:17,550
The rest of India? Empty.

6
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:20,308
Mumbai, Kolkata, Chennai — not a soul.

7
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:24,053
Now bring everyone on Earth, 8.2 billion.

8
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:26,921
The square grows to 64 kilometers.

9
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:30,160
Too big for Delhi, so fly it east into Sikkim,

10
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:32,060
India's least populous state.

11
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:33,994
It fits, with room to spare.

12
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:37,440
So next time someone says India is too crowded, tell them...
